<section class="section">
  <div class="head">
    <h2 class="title sc-reveal">Built for animation, not just eyeballs.</h2>
    <p class="subtitle sc-reveal">Most raster-to-SVG tools give you a single, flattened <code class="inline-code">&lt;path&gt;</code> blob. Spryteo gives you semantic groups and stable IDs, ready for CSS or JS motion.</p>
  </div>
  
  <div class="quality-grid">
    <div class="quality-card sc-reveal">
      <div class="quality-icon">&#9635;</div>
      <h3 class="quality-title">Semantic Grouping</h3>
      <p class="quality-desc">Shapes are hierarchically nested into a proper <code class="inline-code">&lt;g&gt;</code> tree based on containment or mask-guided coverage. Animate the wheel, not the whole car.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="quality-card sc-reveal">
      <div class="quality-icon">&#128274;</div>
      <h3 class="quality-title">Stable Content-Hashed IDs</h3>
      <p class="quality-desc">Every element gets an ID derived from a blake3 hash of its geometry and fill. Tweak your source image and re-export without breaking your animation selectors.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="quality-card sc-reveal">
      <div class="quality-icon">&#128394;</div>
      <h3 class="quality-title">True Centerline Stroke</h3>
      <p class="quality-desc">Use <code class="inline-code">--stroke</code> mode for line art. Instead of outlining a stroke as a filled region, get a true variable-width centerline path with <code class="inline-code">pathLength="100"</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-footer sc-reveal">
    <a href="/docs#options" class="section-docs-link">read more about output quality &#8594;</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 32px;
  }
  .head {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 0 48px;
  }
  .title {
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .subtitle {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .inline-code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 2px 6px;
  }
  
  .quality-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  
  .quality-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 32px;
    transition: transform var(--transition-bounce), border-color var(--transition-fast);
  }
  .quality-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }
  .quality-icon {
    font-size: 28px;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .quality-title {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .quality-desc {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-footer {
    display: flex;
  }
  .section-docs-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--transition-fast);
  }
  .section-docs-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .quality-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .section {
      padding: 64px 20px;
    }
    .title {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
